# Architecture

Standard Laravel layout. Keep controllers thin; put business logic in `app/Services`.

- **No repository layer** — services use Eloquent models/queries directly.
- Validate with Form Requests under `app/Http/Requests/{Domain}/`.
- Map request data to readonly DTOs in `app/Data/{Domain}/` (e.g. `toDTO()`).
- Authorize with Policies + `can:` middleware where ownership/roles matter.
- Bind swappable integrations via Contracts in `app/Contracts` (e.g. `SignatureContract`, `AuditLogContract`) in `AppServiceProvider`.
- API responses: JSON arrays/`JsonResource` collections; prefer `["data" => ...]` / `["success" => true]` patterns already used in the app.
- Domain helpers that are not full services may live under `app/Services/Assistants/`.

```php
// ✅ Controller delegates to service + DTO
public function __invoke(PaymentCreationRequest $request, PaymentCreationService $service)
{
    $url = $service->createPayment($request->toDTO(), $request->header('X-Signature'));
    return response()->json(['data' => ['url' => $url]], 201);
}

// ❌ Fat controller with Eloquent / business rules inline
```
